+//! E2b probe — run-length-table Rice quotient count on the accumulator
+//! reader (**probe code; never lands on `main`'s spike sources**).
+//!
+//! FLAC.md "Perf follow-ups — experiment menu", E2b: E8 attributed the
+//! FIXED arm's cost center to the Rice per-sample loop (unary 56.2% + rest
+//! 38.5% = 94.6% of gross), and the `unary` bucket scales with residual
+//! magnitude — per-**bit** iteration cost. The live loop counts one
+//! `read_bits(1)` per unary bit (E2a proved the reader *implementation* is
+//! not the cost center: swapping to an accumulator moved FIXED only −3.1%).
+//! E2b replaces the per-bit iteration itself with a **run-length-table**
+//! count: the quotient is the leading-zero run, taken 8 bits at a time
+//! from a 256-entry IWRAM-pinned lookup table — no CLZ (ARMv4T/ARM7TDMI
+//! has none; the E2-entry correction), no per-bit loop.
+//!
+//! ## The one variable (arm 3 of the probe)
+//!
+//! The probe measures three arms on one image:
+//!
+//! 1. **ctrl** — `driver::decode_one`, the verbatim live path (control);
+//! 2. **acc** — `e2::decode_one_accumulator` (the E2a sample verbatim):
+//!    accumulator reader, unary loop still per-bit — prices the reader
+//!    swap on this image;
+//! 3. **tab** (this module) — `e2b::decode_one_rice_table`: the *same*
+//!    accumulator reader, but the unary quotient loop is replaced by
+//!    [`AccumulatorReader::rice_quotient`], the table count. The
+//!    **tab − acc** delta is therefore the marginal effect of the count
+//!    change alone; **tab − ctrl** is the composite vs the live baseline.
+//!
+//! Vendor boundary follows the type signatures exactly as E2a's: every
+//! function touching the reader is vendored (header parse, subframe-type
+//! parse, warm-up fill, wasted/coded readers, residual + rice loop);
+//! everything else is a verbatim copy or a shared call (`decorrelate`).
+//! All arithmetic stays **i64 exactly as live** (E4's i32 is NOT merged
+//! and NOT this variable).
+//!
+//! ## The count (the probe's variable)
+//!
+//! `acc` is the E2a left-aligned MSB-first window (next bit = bit 31,
+//! invariant `logical cursor = pos·8 − valid`). The quotient is the run of
+//! leading zeros terminated by a one, so it is the run of leading **ones**
+//! of the inverted window — `LEADING_ONES[!top_byte]` answers runs 0..=8
+//! in one `ldrb` (the table is pinned to `.iwram`: zero-wait data, the
+//! lookup index is data-dependent so a cartridge ROM read would pay a
+//! non-sequential wait per sample; E6's regression was an instruction-
+//! fetch story and does not transfer to hot data — measured here, not
+//! assumed).
+//!
+//! Runs longer than 8 bits iterate **per byte chunk** (~5 cycles per 8
+//! bits instead of per-bit loop iterations): whole-zero byte → quotient
+//! += 8, consume 8, continue. Realistic quotients (E8: the run scales with
+//! residual magnitude, single-digit-to-low-teens bits) resolve in one
+//! lookup.
+//!
+//! Edge semantics:
+//! - **Slice tail** (`valid < 8`): the valid bits are folded to the top of
+//!   the inverted byte with fake terminating ones below, so the table
+//!   answer is capped at `valid`; a run that consumes every remaining bit
+//!   is an unterminated unary → `EndOfStream`.
+//! - **EOF atomicity**: on `EndOfStream` the reader state is restored to
+//!   the word start (snapshot). The live per-bit loop leaves the cursor
+//!   after the consumed zeros (per-read atomicity, frame discarded
+//!   either way — residual.rs cursor contract); the difference is only
+//!   observable on a corrupt stream, where the frame is dead on both
+//!   paths. Never fires on the committed clips (witnessed bit-exact).
+//! - **Consume-and-remainder**: once `q` is known, `q + 1` bits vanish in
+//!   one shift pair and the `order` remainder bits are extracted from the
+//!   same window — the fold/unmap/guard rules below stay verbatim live.
+//!
+//! ## Witness chain (before any number counts)
+//!
+//! 1. Host (`tests/e2b_witness.rs`): this vendored path decodes the exact
+//!    embedded clips bit-exactly vs the `flac -d` reference PCM, and
+//!    differentially frame-by-frame against the production
+//!    `driver::decode_one`.
+//! 2. Host unit tests (this file): the table is exhaustively checked
+//!    against a naive leading-ones count; the count is swept over
+//!    quotient lengths 0..=40 at every bit offset 0..7, against a naive
+//!    per-bit oracle, plus EOF (unterminated run) cursor restoration and
+//!    reader mixed-width differential (the copy never drifted).
+//! 3. ROM: per-frame **sample-equality** of both variant arms against
+//!    the control (E1/E2a/E4 pattern); first offender named; divergence
+//!    voids the numbers.
+//! 4. Link witness (offline, pre-measurement): `nm` on the built ELF —
+//!    the table symbol lands in `0x0300xxxx` (the `.iwram` section,
+//!    copied ROM→IWRAM at boot by agb's `CommonInit` CPUSet); the boot
+//!    log echoes the runtime address as the same-image echo.
+
+// E2b placement allowances (probe branch only; see module docs).
+// Edition-2024 + this nightly treat `link_section` as an unsafe attribute:
+// any use fires `unsafe_code` (deny after the probe's lib.rs change) and
+// bare use also fires `unsafe_attr_outside_unsafe`. The attribute pins the
+// 256 B lookup table to `.iwram`, gated to the bare-metal target; the host
+// witness build never sees it. No actual unsafe CODE exists in this module.
+#![allow(unsafe_code, unsafe_attr_outside_unsafe)]
+
+use crate::assets::SpikeClip;
+use crate::driver::DriverError;
+use flac_lite::format::{ChannelConfig, SampleRate};
+use flac_lite::frame::{FrameHeader, StreamDefaults};
+use flac_lite::residual::PartitionHeader;
