+//! witness `spike_witness.rs` runs for the production path and
+//! `e2_witness.rs` runs for the E2a accumulator arm.
+//!
+//! Second layer: a differential frame-by-frame sample comparison against
+//! the production `driver::decode_one` on the same bytes — the host twin
+//! of the ROM's per-frame equality witness. The equivalence claim (module
+//! docs of `e2b.rs`): the table count replaces only *how* the unary
+//! quotient is counted, never *which* bits are consumed — so bit-exact
+//! agreement with both the encoder ground truth and the live loop is the
+//! machine check of that claim on real frames.
+//!
+//! Sample code, never lands on `main`'s spike sources (see
+//! `experiments/e2b-rice-quotient-table/`).
